I: Functions
-> All function arguments must be type hinted
-> All functions must be type labeled if they return anything
-> Pass arguments only by keyword
-> Raise errors instead of returning None

II: Naming
-> All functions are named as verbs
-> Functions that return something are of the format get_[object]. Ideally the name of the function
should make the type of the returned object apparent already
-> Plural with "object_list" not "objects"

-> private attributes should be of the form "_[attribute]" so that they are properly hidden

III: Contracts
-> Every module (class) has to have contracts for both its attributes its methods
-> That arguments are of the type they are hinted to be is a default assumption of every contract


IV: Making changes
-> Any change that you make has to either not influence the contract of that section of code or
the changes to the contract have to be carried through upstream





